{
  "$comment": "RPLumen: reverse Polish Lumen. A program is a sequence of words acting on one stack: a literal pushes itself, an operator pops its operands and pushes the result (5 3 + is 5 + 3), a quoted name 'x' is data for the word after it, which must take a name (8 'x' = assigns, 4 'arr' push appends), a bare word pushes its variable's value or runs the program stored under it, and « ... » is a program value. Control words delimit bodies as on the HP-48: cond if ... else ... end, while cond repeat body end, do body until cond end, start stop 'i' for body next. Same numbers, strings and arrays as Lumen; print and write are kernel builtins here because the Lumen library is written in infix Lumen.",
